+### 1.3 Actionable Findings for Group 1
+
+#### Finding G1-01: Single Synthetic Native Timeout Measurement
+- **Severity**: Low (Measurement Limit)
+- **Path & Context**: `_scratch/asr-dummy-worker-timeout02/controller-result.json`
+- **Trigger**: Native timeout02 measures exactly one timeout event (250 ms wait, elapsed 0.255 s) on a single dummy child worker.
+- **Consequence**: While synthetic controls (67 cases) verify 109/995/996 logic across memory mocks, native behavior is established for only one specific timing window. It does not measure multi-threaded overlapped cancellations, high-concurrency pipe teardown, or arbitrary process termination timing.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: Maintain explicit documentation that native broken-pipe retirement is qualified solely for the controlled generated dummy worker, not general native runtime I/O.
+
+#### Finding G1-02: Physical Teardown Must Not Apply to Shared or Production Assets
+- **Severity**: Low (Architecture Boundary)
+- **Path & Line**: `_scratch/asr-dummy-worker-timeout02/generated_worker_flow.py#L216-L244` (`teardown_generated_handles`)
+- **Trigger**: Calling `teardown_generated_handles` closes Win32 handles while keeping the lifecycle record quarantined.
+- **Consequence**: In a production environment with shared read sets or persistent caches, forcibly closing handles without durable quarantine persistence could cause resource desynchronization or release untracked locks.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: Restrict physical handle teardown to isolated, disposable test fixtures. Production recovery must require durable quarantine persistence before handle reclamation.
+
+#### Finding G1-03: Child Readback Scope Limited to Fixture Data
+- **Severity**: Low (Data & Model Scope Limit)
+- **Path & Line**: `_scratch/child-readset-positive01/inherited_readset.py#L12-L16`
+- **Trigger**: Materialization reads 328 bytes across five ASCII files (`config.json`, `model.bin`, `preprocessor_config.json`, `tokenizer.json`, `vocabulary.json`).
+- **Consequence**: `model.bin` contains 60 bytes of ASCII text, not binary neural network weights. No real model deserialization, memory mapping, or native execution occurred.
+- **Smallest Repair / Missing Observation**: Explicitly record that child adoption qualifies file descriptor passing and byte readback, not model loading or inference.
